# Expectation record for 03_initializers/008_union_initializers.c
#
# Union initialization and designated union members, including one deliberate and
# fully justified union type-pun that observes an object representation.
#
# Reproduce one cell by hand with no harness: render the three command templates
# below, substituting the target triple, the optimization level, the source path,
# the output path, and the target's runner (empty on the natively executing target).

program            = 008_union_initializers
area               = 03_initializers
description        = Union initialization and designated union members -- unlabelled initialization of the first member, designated scalar aggregate and array members, a partially initialized array member, a union with an array member using a nested designator, a designator descending through a struct into a union member, an array of unions mixing designated and positional element initializers, and one justified union type-pun -- for static and automatic storage duration, every member read back individually
targets            = x86_64, i686, aarch64, riscv64
opt_levels         = -O0, -O1, -O2
shared_flags       = -static
bcc_command        = $BCC --target <triple> <opt> -static <src> -o <out>
ref_command        = $REF_CC_<TRIPLE> <opt> -static <src> -o <out>
run_command        = <runner> <out>
expect_exit        = 0
oracle_a           = enabled
oracle_b           = enabled
oracle_c           = enabled
ub_notes           <<END
This program contains no undefined and no unspecified behaviour, which is the precondition that
makes both differential oracles sound: undefined behaviour would license either compiler to do
anything at all, so a divergence over it would prove nothing about either one.
AN UNLABELLED UNION INITIALIZER INITIALIZES THE FIRST MEMBER of the union, which C11 6.7.9p17
fixes. g_first = { 5 }, g_uarr[2] = { 53 } and l_first = { 61 } rely on that rule and read back .i
accordingly, so a front end that selected some other member surfaces here as a wrong value rather
than as an unobserved reinterpretation.
EVERY UNION EXCEPT g_pun IS READ THROUGH EXACTLY THE MEMBER ITS INITIALIZER SET. g_first,
g_desig_i, g_uarr[0], g_uarr[2], g_holder.u and l_first set and read .i; g_desig_u and g_uarr[1]
set and read .u; g_desig_s and l_desig_s set and read .s; g_desig_b and g_desig_b_pt set and read
.b; g_arr_whole, g_arr_desig and l_arr_desig set and read .a. No other member of any of those
unions is inspected, so no padding byte is observed and no object representation is relied upon.
THE ONE DELIBERATE TYPE-PUN IS FULLY JUSTIFIED. g_pun is initialized { .i = 0x01020304 } and read
back through the unsigned char array member b as 4, 3, 2, 1. Four separate facts make this well
defined and target-invariant:
  - Reading a union member other than the one last stored is permitted in C. C11 6.5.2.3 and its
    footnote 95 explicitly sanction using a union to reinterpret an object representation. This is
    not the undefined case that a cast between unrelated struct pointer types would be, and no
    pointer cast is used -- the reinterpretation is performed solely by union member access, which
    is the sanctioned mechanism.
  - No padding byte is observed. sizeof(int) is 4 and b is exactly unsigned char[4], so the four
    bytes read are precisely the four bytes of the int. Padding contents are unspecified, which is
    why this matters.
  - unsigned char has no trap representations, so each of the four bytes has a well-defined value.
  - All four supported targets are little-endian and have a 4-byte int, so the byte order 4, 3, 2,
    1 is the result on every backend. See impl_defined_notes.
The value is read immediately, with nothing modified in between.
NO READ OF UNINITIALIZED STORAGE, which is what makes the zero lines assertions rather than
accidents. Where an initializer names only some elements of an array member --
g_desig_b_pt = { .b = { 9 } }, g_arr_desig = { .a = { [2] = 33 } } and
l_arr_desig = { .a = { [1] = 82 } } -- the unnamed elements are implicitly initialized to zero
under C11 6.7.9p19 and p21, for automatic duration exactly as for static, because an object with
any initializer at all is fully initialized. So g_desig_b_pt.b[1..3], g_arr_desig.a[0..1] and
l_arr_desig.a[0] and a[2] each hold a determinate value of zero.
NO MEMBER RECEIVES TWO INITIALIZERS. Each union in this program is initialized through exactly one
member, and g_holder's designators .tag, .u.i and .trailer address three distinct members of the
enclosing struct. There is therefore no overlapping or overriding initializer anywhere. An
overlapping union member designator such as { .i = 1, .u = 2 } is deliberately absent: measurement
established that -Woverride-init, enabled by -Wextra and promoted to a hard error by -Werror,
rejects every value-overriding designator spelling, that union pairing among them. That exclusion
and its full reasoning are recorded in 004_designated_array.expected, which is the program whose
subject is designator precedence. Area 03 sanctions no deviation from the default gate, so no
`ub_audit_flags` override is used here, and none is needed.
ANONYMOUS UNIONS ARE DELIBERATELY NOT EXERCISED HERE; they are the subject of area 10, program
010_anonymous_struct_union. Naming where the construct is covered is what keeps its absence from
this program a division of labour rather than a gap in the corpus.
No arithmetic is performed on any initialized value, so signed overflow is impossible. The only
run-time arithmetic is on the loop counter i, bounded i < 4 over b[4] and i < 3 over a[3], so every
subscript is strictly in bounds; no one-past-the-end pointer is even formed, let alone
dereferenced. There is no shift of any kind, no division and no remainder. No object is modified
after its initialization, so nothing is modified twice between two sequence points. No pointer is
cast anywhere, so there is no aliasing violation, and beyond the one sanctioned union access every
value is read through an lvalue of its own declared type: int through int, unsigned through
unsigned, and unsigned char through unsigned char. No address is taken and none is printed, and
nothing depends on the relative addresses of unrelated objects.
Each printf call passes at most one loop counter and one already-narrowed value, neither with a
side effect, so the unspecified order in which a function call's arguments are evaluated cannot be
observed. %d takes int -- including every (int)-cast unsigned char and every (int)sizeof -- and %u
takes unsigned int, matching after the default argument promotions, so no variadic argument is read
at the wrong width. 0x01020304 is representable in a 32-bit int, and 4000000000u and 52u in a
32-bit unsigned int, on every supported target, so no implementation-defined conversion occurs.
main returns 0, inside the 0-125 range the suite requires so that no exit status is truncated by
the operating system. Output is fully deterministic: fixed iteration order, no address, no
timestamp, no randomness and no locale-dependent formatting, and nothing outside this file is read,
so every cell is reproducible from this source and this record alone.
No header is included anywhere and no preprocessor directive appears at all; printf is declared by
hand as `int printf(const char *, ...);`. bcc bundles the nine required freestanding headers plus a
bonus stdatomic.h and ships no standard I/O header (docs/project-guide.md line 212), so naming one
would fail on the bcc side of oracle (a) while succeeding on the reference side -- a spurious
divergence caused by the test rather than by a compiler. This area is granted no header exception;
the corpus has exactly two, area 07's stdarg.h and the dedicated bundled-header probe in area 12.
This record declares no warning-gate deviation, and area 03 sanctions none. The program was
MEASURED clean under the full default gate -Wall -Wextra -pedantic -Wconversion -Wsign-conversion
-Wshadow -Werror at -O0, -O1 and -O2 with all four reference drivers, and it builds and runs clean
under the sanitizer gate -fsanitize=undefined,address -fno-sanitize-recover=all, emitting these
same 38 lines with an empty standard error. Both gates are reference-compiler-only and are never
applied to bcc, so requirement 3's shared-flag discipline is untouched.
END
impl_defined_notes <<END
This record narrows nothing: all four targets, all three optimization levels and all three oracles
are enabled, no expected-divergence marker is carried, and no `ub_audit_flags` key appears because
the program passes the suite's full default warning gate unmodified. The field is present anyway,
because this program observes an object representation, and what makes that safe belongs somewhere
a reader will find it rather than nowhere at all.
ENDIANNESS IS OBSERVED HERE, DELIBERATELY AND EXACTLY ONCE. g_pun reinterprets a four-byte int
through an unsigned char[4], so the printed byte order depends on the target's byte order. All
four supported targets are little-endian -- recorded in the authoritative target table
(docs/technical-specifications.md lines 457-462, whose four target rows each read "Little") and
independently MEASURED on each of them -- and int is 4 bytes on all four, so 0x01020304 reads back
as 4, 3, 2, 1 on every backend. This is the only place in this feature area that observes an
object representation, which makes it a direct cross-backend check on union member placement
rather than an accident, and it is why oracle (b) stays ENABLED for this program despite the pun:
byte order is uniform across the four targets, so a divergence in that line group would be a
genuine finding about union member layout rather than an implementation-defined difference, and it
is deliberately not a marker candidate.
ALL sizeof VALUES ARE TARGET-INVARIANT. sizeof_simple is 4, sizeof_mixed is 8 and sizeof_witharr
is 12. Each follows solely from int being 4 bytes with 4-byte alignment and unsigned char being 1
byte, which holds on all four targets: union mixed is the maximum of int at 4, struct pair at 8 and
unsigned char[4] at 4, and union witharr is the maximum of int at 4 and int[3] at 12. Each of the
three sizes was MEASURED on each of the four targets. The shapes were chosen so that no padding
depends on the alignment of a type whose alignment is 4 on i686 and 8 elsewhere.
WIDTHS ARE NORMALIZED. Every printed value is an int or an unsigned int, printed with %d or %u
alone and with every unsigned char cast to int first. No pointer, no long and no size_t is ever
measured or printed and no floating type is used anywhere, so nothing here depends on the MEASURED
pointer-width difference on i686 -- four bytes there against eight on x86-64, AArch64 and RISC-V 64
-- and no address or pointer value is printed. The source comment deliberately avoids NAMING those
excluded types so that a portability audit grep over this program reports a hit only for a genuine
use; that convention is recorded here rather than repeated there.
PLAIN-CHAR SIGNEDNESS CANNOT AFFECT THIS PROGRAM. The byte-array member b is declared explicitly as
unsigned char, never as plain char, and its elements are promoted to int by an explicit cast before
printing, so the MEASURED split -- signed on x86-64 and i686, unsigned on AArch64 and RISC-V 64 --
has no way to influence any printed value.
EXECUTION CHARACTER SET. No character literal value is printed; the unsigned char bytes printed are
the object representation of an integer, not characters.
THE STATIC/AUTOMATIC PAIRING IS THIS PROGRAM'S DISCRIMINATING VARIANT, and it was verified at
INSTRUCTION level rather than assumed. At -O0 all eleven static objects receive real data images:
g_pun as one four-byte word holding 16909060, g_desig_b as four one-byte values 1, 2, 3 and 4,
g_desig_b_pt as one byte 9 followed by three zero bytes, g_arr_desig as eight zero bytes followed by
the word 33, and g_holder as the three words 41, 42 and 43 in that order; and the three automatic
twins are initialized by stores into the frame. At -O2 not one static object survives -- every value
is folded into an immediate operand of the call that prints it. So -O0 exercises the
initializer-emission path and -O2 the constant-folding path over the same declarations, and both must
produce the recorded bytes. A volatile operand would add nothing here, because the subject is what an
initializer produces rather than what an operator computes -- which is why this program carries no
volatile variant and needs none.
WHERE THE SHAPES DO EXTRA WORK. g_holder is bracketed by tag and trailer so that a designator- or
layout-resolution error shifts one of them rather than only the union member, and each element of
g_uarr is read through the member its own initializer stored -- i, then u, then i again for the
positional element -- so a wrong member selection surfaces as a wrong value rather than as an
unobserved reinterpretation.
MEASURED EVIDENCE. The program was compiled with the reference driver for all four targets at -O0,
-O1 and -O2 -- twelve configurations -- and every one produced these 38 lines byte-identically with
exit status 0, which is why oracle (b) compares this program's targets against each other without
any narrowing and why oracle (c) can hold these bytes as the golden record. Every member and element
is printed on its own line, including the elements an initializer leaves implicitly zero, so a single
divergent line localizes the defect to one initializer form rather than to "one of them".
What would legitimately break these bytes is a big-endian target, which would reverse the four
g_pun.b lines without being defective, or a target where sizeof(int) were not 4, which would change
both the reinterpretation and the three printed sizes. Either would be an implementation-defined
divergence rather than a compiler defect, and must then be recorded as an expected divergence with
this record's target list narrowed and the reason stated in this field -- never left to surface as
a finding against a backend that did nothing wrong, and never resolved by deleting the
reinterpretation or dropping the union coverage this program exists to provide. None of the four
supported targets is big-endian, so no such narrowing is carried today.
END
expected_stdout    <<END
g_first.i=5
g_desig_i.i=-7
g_desig_u.u=4000000000
g_desig_s.s.p=11
g_desig_s.s.q=12
g_desig_b.b[0]=1
g_desig_b.b[1]=2
g_desig_b.b[2]=3
g_desig_b.b[3]=4
g_desig_b_pt.b[0]=9
g_desig_b_pt.b[1]=0
g_desig_b_pt.b[2]=0
g_desig_b_pt.b[3]=0
g_pun.b[0]=4
g_pun.b[1]=3
g_pun.b[2]=2
g_pun.b[3]=1
g_arr_whole.a[0]=21
g_arr_whole.a[1]=22
g_arr_whole.a[2]=23
g_arr_desig.a[0]=0
g_arr_desig.a[1]=0
g_arr_desig.a[2]=33
g_holder.tag=41
g_holder.u.i=42
g_holder.trailer=43
g_uarr[0].i=51
g_uarr[1].u=52
g_uarr[2].i=53
sizeof_simple=4
sizeof_mixed=8
sizeof_witharr=12
l_first.i=61
l_desig_s.s.p=71
l_desig_s.s.q=72
l_arr_desig.a[0]=0
l_arr_desig.a[1]=82
l_arr_desig.a[2]=0
END
